hey guys it's angelico with max tech and  i just upgraded to an iphone 13 pro from  my 10r that i've had for years now and  i've gotta say it's been long overdue  this phone has been the subject of my  dreams every night for the past six  months ever since vadim made his first  iphone 13 leaks video and going from  something like my 10r which is now  officially discontinued by apple to this  phone is a crazy upgrade so in this  video i'm going to talk about all the  changes i've experienced so far  switching to this 13 pro both good and  bad and then i'm gonna get into how it's  changed my day-to-day life as an average  consumer and if it's worth coughing up  the dough this year if you currently  have a much older iphone like the 10r  let's start off with the most obvious  difference and that is the square design  i love the flush display and flat  stainless steel sides of the pros they  really stand out and make the phone look  like a slab of premium if premium were a  noun to this day sometimes i stop what  i'm doing and i just sit there admiring  the new design it almost looks too nice  for me to own especially side by side  with my 10r even though on paper it  doesn't look like much in the hand i can  feel a considerable weight difference  for me this is a slight disadvantage  because it's definitely less comfortable  to lay down and watch movies for long  periods of time and i'm now deathly  afraid of dropping this phone on my face  let's move on to the feature that made  me want to upgrade in the first place  and that is promotion i absolutely love  this feature everything is so smooth and  so crisp it's so much easier on the eyes  and it looks fantastic and switching  made anything that uses 60 hertz look  terrible and it is impossible not to  notice the difference now promotion is  something interesting and that to me and  pretty much everyone into tech it is a  huge deal and a really big reason to  upgrade but for most casual consumers it  doesn't really matter joshua chang made  a video where he brought in five of his  friends and gave them 13 pros to play  with and see if they notice a difference  in refresh rate  and out of the five only one person  noticed without help from joshua and  when asked if they would upgrade for  this feature the consensus was that it's  great and looks nice but it's not  something worth paying the money for  this is better i suppose but like  not enough for me to like really  complain about it from my phone and  that's absolutely true you do not need  it it looks and it feels great and i was  very excited for it but is it really  that important for the average user  probably not unless you want to do 120  fps mobile gaming a great thing about  promotion though is that it improves  battery life because the refresh rate  adapts in real time and can go down to  10 hertz you're saving battery life  compared to it being locked at 60 hertz  and i know a lot of you may say that hey  samsung smartphones like the s21 ultra  have already had this feature so it's  not really impressive but the thing is  that the s21 ultra actually wastes  battery life it's advertised as being  able to go down to 10 hertz as well  but users have noticed that on static  images it stays at 60 hertz and it only  goes down to 48 hertz when viewing 20  fps video and some people have tested  the always on display and apparently it  also stays at 60 hertz now before i get  into my real world experience with  battery life on this 13 pro compared to  my old 10r i want to ask you guys to  subscribe because apparently only around  23 percent of you are  and with that you can help us reach our  goal of 1 million subscribers before the  end of the year we'd really appreciate  it back to battery life it is insane  ever since i got the 13 pro i have not  once put it in battery saving mode  during weekdays at work i keep it on a  wireless charger so it's always topped  off and one day after typical use for me  at night before i went to bed my phone  was at 82 percent the crazy thing is i  don't even have to charge it at night on  weekends i use carplay when i drive  which simultaneously charges my phone  and topping off just from driving is  enough to keep my battery alive the  entire weekend this is incredible never  having to worry about battery life when  on my 10r i almost always had to have it  on battery saving mode and still charge  at night this is one of the biggest  things that makes it worth upgrading  especially if you have a much older  phone that you've had for years since  battery health will decline over time  the next thing i was excited for was the  smaller notch now this isn't a big deal  as it's still a mammoth compared to  literally every notch out there  but it's nice to not have it cut into  videos as much it's just been something  that we've been waiting for for years  and it finally distinguishes itself  apart from previous iphone models on the  front hopefully one day with a software  update the extra space given will be  utilized like showing your actual  battery percentage i do also really like  how the layout has changed with the  speaker grille being moved to the top of  the notch instead of in the center it  definitely makes it look much neater  however according to analyst ross young  the next iphone 14 will get rid of the  notch entirely and have a hole punch  just like most current android phones  which is going to be a game changer  especially since face id will still  likely be implemented  just under the display and speaking of  the display in real world i have noticed  a massive difference for one the 13 pro  has an oled display compared to an lcd  in the 10r with a ppi of 460 compared to  326  so it's very sharp with high contrast  but what's crazy between these is the  difference in brightness this year for  the first time the 13 pro models have a  peak typical brightness of 1000 nits  compared to the previous 800 but my 10r  has a peak of 625  that difference sounds insane and it  looks insane too i'm finally able to use  my phone outside in the sun and be able  to see what i'm doing when before i  never could especially because my 10r  would constantly dim from the heat of  the sun and speaking of dimming i have  not experienced it happening even once  so far with my 10r it would constantly  overheat and sometimes the display would  even them down to 30 percent indoors and  i don't even do things that draw crazy  amounts of power like gaming i've also  noticed a massive difference in the  speakers they are so much louder and  clearer and i can finally play music  from my phone and it's loud enough for  my liking when before i'd exclusively  use my airpods because the speakers on  the 10r were just way too quiet another  huge improvement that i'm extremely  happy about  is the increase in ram the pro models of  the 12 and 13s finally come with six  gigabytes of ram compared to four  gigabytes on all the other models and  that extra 50 changes everything it was  a constant pain having my apps refresh  every time i open them even if i only  had like three or four open and now i  finally no longer have to deal with that  problem and it is such a relief nothing  is more annoying than having a youtube  video on opening another app to check  something and having youtube refresh on  you moving on something i know a lot of  people are curious about are the  cellular speeds so we ran a test outside  and the download speed went from 52  megabytes per second to 206 and the  upload went from seven megabytes per  second to 28. literally being four times  faster in both now there are a few more  improvements that i haven't had time to  fully explore but i'm really excited to  and one of those are the cameras now  both the 10 and the 10s have dual  cameras a wide and a telephoto but i had  a 10r and that only has a single wide  lens the photo quality was pretty  terrible last month i went on a trip to  olympic national park and i was so  bummed to still have my 10r the photos  weren't so bad during the day but as it  got darker on my hike the photo quality  got worse and worse here is an out of  focus shot just for reference of how  dark it was and here is a portrait photo  i tried to take that looks like  something straight out of a horror movie  portrait photos especially nighttime got  a huge improvement this year so i'm  really excited to finally be able to get  good looking photos the last feature  that i haven't been able to utilize yet  but i'm really excited for is magsafe  there are so many accessories that i'm  already planning on purchasing just like  belkin's two-in-one charger stand from  my phone and airpods pro and this sticky  wall mount from amazon that we featured  in one of our top magsafe accessories  videos i'm planning on buying a few of  these to use when doing things like  cooking or working out you can also use  this as a simple and clean wall mount in  your car so i know the price tag of 999  is pretty hefty but this iphone 13 pro  has fully lived up to my expectations  and i am beyond thrilled to own this  phone gorgeous design 120 hertz insane  battery life and 6 gigs of ram makes  this phone more than worth it and that's  not even mentioning the insane camera  differences which alone are worth it so  if you have an older iphone and you're  wondering if this is the year to upgrade  i would personally say it depends on how  excited you are about these features if  you're like me and you've been waiting  for features like 120 hertz then  absolutely go for it i know you love  this phone as much as i do as a regular  consumer and if you really want the 14  that's coming next year i'm in the same  boat which is why i signed up for the  upgrade program don't forget that you  always have the option to pick up this  13 and then sell it next year when the  14 comes out so with all of that said i  hope this video helped you if you have  an older iphone like i did click the  button above to subscribe and go ahead  and check out one of those two videos  over there this has been angelica with  max tech thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

